  BIT-115. Small icon for the swap Live Update, phase `complete`.
  check_circle, FILL 1 — iOS `checkmark.circle.fill`.

  Material Symbols, weight 400, grade 0, optical size 24, **FILL 1**. Filled rather than
  outlined on purpose: `setSmallIcon` is rendered at status-bar size, where the 2dp strokes
  of an outlined glyph break up. That is why iOS's outlined `hourglass` does not port as
  `hourglass_empty`.

  **This is an alpha silhouette, not a coloured icon.** On a colorized notification the
  framework paints the small icon in the palette's primary text colour
  (`Notification.Colors#getPrimaryTextColor`, measured at #1A1B20 over our #FFC502 tint), so
  the fillColor below is discarded at render time. White is declared only so the glyph is
  visible in the tooling preview. Every piece of detail is a transparent cut-out; do not add
  a second colour to any of these five, it will not survive.

  Material Symbols are authored on a 960x960 grid with a y-up viewBox ("0 -960 960 960"),
  which VectorDrawable has no equivalent for. The group's translateY is that offset, so the
  path data below is byte-identical to the upstream glyph and can be re-synced without
  re-deriving coordinates.
-->
